{
  "$comment": "Beats are the sections of the paper. The research skill works this list top to bottom. `quota` is the target number of stories per edition for the edited paper; `minQuota` is the floor below which the edition is still publishable. `digestQuota` is the separate, much larger cap for the no-AI Tier 1.5 digest — a headline aggregator should carry far more per beat than a written paper does, and reusing `quota` there capped the digest at nine items regardless of how much news existed. `keywords` is the classifier vocabulary used by tools/lib/classify.mjs; `queries` are WebSearch seeds for the editorial research stage. Those were the same list until 18 Aug 2026, which meant the classifier was matching real headlines against a handful of search phrases and discarding 59% of genuinely AI-relevant items — including a $7bn acquisition.",
